{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012LCGwL8nSm8iDa4b51Ty71","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Andreis König Patterson \"large-deviations principle for all the cluster sizes of a sparse Erdős–Rényi graph\" arXiv\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"www.wias-berlin.de\",\"url\":\"https://www.wias-berlin.de/people/koenig/www/AKP19Revision.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"iris.unito.it\",\"url\":\"https://iris.unito.it/handle/2318/2101034\"},{\"title\":\"flore.unifi.it\",\"url\":\"https://flore.unifi.it/handle/2158/1246921\"},{\"title\":\"polimi.it\",\"url\":\"https://re.public.polimi.it/retrieve/a8e4df89-832f-4189-9732-25fbf7bd96fd/rsa.21007.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"oa.tib.eu\",\"url\":\"https://oa.tib.eu/renate/server/api/core/bitstreams/3df73297-b74f-42b5-87ec-a7c59bbf85da/content\"},{\"title\":\"A large‐deviations principle for all the cluster sizes of a sparse Erdős–Rényi graph\",\"url\":\"https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8e5a1020-e0f4-4aa7-88e0-59c06d0a56d5/full\"},{\"title\":\"re.public.polimi.it\",\"url\":\"https://re.public.polimi.it/handle/11311/1224578\"},{\"title\":\"InhomogGraphLDP Springer\",\"url\":\"https://wias-berlin.de:8443/people/koenig/www/InhomogGraphLDP_Springer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"8e5a1020 e0f4 4aa7 88e0 59c06d0a56d5\",\"url\":\"https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8e5a1020-e0f4-4aa7-88e0-59c06d0a56d5\"},{\"title\":\"A large-deviations principle for all the cluster sizes of a sparse Erdős-Rényi graph\",\"url\":\"https://oa.tib.eu/renate/items/67122b81-9f6b-4018-b399-291180d5328f/full\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return an arXiv listing, but it did find the paper and its preprint. It's by Luisa Andreis, Wolfgang König, and Robert I. A. Patterson, and appeared in *Random Structures & Algorithms* in 2021 (vol. 59, no. 4, pp. 522–553, DOI 10.1002/rsa.21007). A preprint version dated August 2020 is hosted on Wolfgang König's WIAS Berlin page.\n\nThe paper studies the Erdős–Rényi graph with connection probability t/N for fixed t > 0. It proves a large-deviations principle for the empirical measure of all connected-component sizes. The authors sort components into microscopic (finite), mesoscopic, and macroscopic (order N) classes. The rate function is explicit. The result also captures the phase transition at t = 1. The authors draw consequences for the multiplicative coalescent, the Marcus–Lushnikov model with monodisperse initial condition, and gelation.\n\nSources: the [WIAS preprint](https://www.wias-berlin.de/people/koenig/www/AKP19Revision.pdf), the [journal version at Polimi](https://re.public.polimi.it/retrieve/a8e4df89-832f-4189-9732-25fbf7bd96fd/rsa.21007.pdf), and the [TU Berlin deposit record](https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8e5a1020-e0f4-4aa7-88e0-59c06d0a56d5/full), which gives the DOI and page numbers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d0376bd-2c82-42d0-bb0a-a9a308847d25","uuid":"35c38fb1-f8e6-4a82-b0d2-607adce3f312","timestamp":"2026-11-01T12:38:20.456Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Andreis König Patterson \"large-deviations principle for all the cluster sizes of a sparse Erdős–Rényi graph\" arXiv","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015JdX5nMwRjsf3XNDQdG697","content":[{"title":"www.wias-berlin.de","url":"https://www.wias-berlin.de/people/koenig/www/AKP19Revision.pdf"},{"title":"iris.unito.it","url":"https://iris.unito.it/handle/2318/2101034"},{"title":"flore.unifi.it","url":"https://flore.unifi.it/handle/2158/1246921"},{"title":"polimi.it","url":"https://re.public.polimi.it/retrieve/a8e4df89-832f-4189-9732-25fbf7bd96fd/rsa.21007.pdf"},{"title":"oa.tib.eu","url":"https://oa.tib.eu/renate/server/api/core/bitstreams/3df73297-b74f-42b5-87ec-a7c59bbf85da/content"},{"title":"A large‐deviations principle for all the cluster sizes of a sparse Erdős–Rényi graph","url":"https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8e5a1020-e0f4-4aa7-88e0-59c06d0a56d5/full"},{"title":"re.public.polimi.it","url":"https://re.public.polimi.it/handle/11311/1224578"},{"title":"InhomogGraphLDP Springer","url":"https://wias-berlin.de:8443/people/koenig/www/InhomogGraphLDP_Springer.pdf"},{"title":"8e5a1020 e0f4 4aa7 88e0 59c06d0a56d5","url":"https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8e5a1020-e0f4-4aa7-88e0-59c06d0a56d5"},{"title":"A large-deviations principle for all the cluster sizes of a sparse Erdős-Rényi graph","url":"https://oa.tib.eu/renate/items/67122b81-9f6b-4018-b399-291180d5328f/full"}]},"The search didn't return an arXiv listing, but it did find the paper and its preprint. It's by Luisa Andreis, Wolfgang König, and Robert I. A. Patterson, and appeared in *Random Structures & Algorithms* in 2021 (vol. 59, no. 4, pp. 522–553, DOI 10.1002/rsa.21007). A preprint version dated August 2020 is hosted on Wolfgang König's WIAS Berlin page.\n\nThe paper studies the Erdős–Rényi graph with connection probability t/N for fixed t > 0. It proves a large-deviations principle for the empirical measure of all connected-component sizes. The authors sort components into microscopic (finite), mesoscopic, and macroscopic (order N) classes. The rate function is explicit. The result also captures the phase transition at t = 1. The authors draw consequences for the multiplicative coalescent, the Marcus–Lushnikov model with monodisperse initial condition, and gelation.\n\nSources: the [WIAS preprint](https://www.wias-berlin.de/people/koenig/www/AKP19Revision.pdf), the [journal version at Polimi](https://re.public.polimi.it/retrieve/a8e4df89-832f-4189-9732-25fbf7bd96fd/rsa.21007.pdf), and the [TU Berlin deposit record](https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8e5a1020-e0f4-4aa7-88e0-59c06d0a56d5/full), which gives the DOI and page numbers."],"durationSeconds":5.669297312000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012LCGwL8nSm8iDa4b51Ty71","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3x4XTdZEJ9UK6rPGmWFkU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"O'Connell 1998 \"Some large deviation results for sparse random graphs\" Probability Theory and Related Fields pdf\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A large-deviations principle for all the components in a sparse inhomogeneous random graph\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.13200\"},{\"title\":\"An introduction to large deviations for random graphs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1604.06828\"},{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s004400050149\"},{\"title\":\"Some large deviation results for sparse random graphs\",\"url\":\"https://www.readinglength.com/work/WRK929l\"},{\"title\":\"Large deviations of empirical neighborhood distribution in sparse random graphs\",\"url\":\"https://academicnewsletter.sufe.edu.cn/info/430372\"},{\"title\":\"Large deviations of empirical neighborhood distribution in sparse random graphs\",\"url\":\"https://uniroma3.academia.edu/PietroCaputo\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0402183\"},{\"title\":\"A large-deviations principle for all the components in a sparse inhomogeneous random graph\",\"url\":\"https://academicnewsletter.sufe.edu.cn/info/429751\"},{\"title\":\"Large deviations of empirical neighborhood distribution in sparse random graphs\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/1308.5725\"},{\"title\":\"On the large deviation rate function for marked sparse random graphs\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2312.16103\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a free PDF of the paper itself, but it did find the publisher's page, which has the abstract and citation details.\n\n- **Citation:** The Springer record gives the paper as Probability Theory and Related Fields, volume 110, pages 277–285 (1998), with DOI 10.1007/s004400050149. It also has an \"Article PDF\" link, so the full text is likely available there, possibly behind a paywall. (Springer lists the article under O'Connell, N., in Probab Theory Relat Fields 110, 277–285 (1998), with DOI 10.1007/s004400050149.)\n- **Abstract:** The paper establishes a large deviation principle for the relative size of the largest connected component in a sparse random graph, with the rate function computed explicitly. It also gives an asymptotic formula for the probability that the graph is connected, and an LDP for the number of isolated vertices (the rate function is not convex in general and is determined explicitly using a new technique, and the proof yields an asymptotic formula for the probability that the random graph is connected).\n- **Related work:** Later papers cite this one as an early result in the area. For example, Chatterjee's survey on large deviations for random graphs covers the sparse case (the remainder of that paper is devoted to large deviations for sparse graphs).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d0376bd-2c82-42d0-bb0a-a9a308847d25","uuid":"0698062b-bc47-4846-a040-9984d52e77f4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T12:38:20.904Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"O'Connell 1998 \"Some large deviation results for sparse random graphs\" Probability Theory and Related Fields pdf","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018HFDqro2euRe1RLqquP6tZ","content":[{"title":"A large-deviations principle for all the components in a sparse inhomogeneous random graph","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.13200"},{"title":"An introduction to large deviations for random graphs","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1604.06828"},{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s004400050149"},{"title":"Some large deviation results for sparse random graphs","url":"https://www.readinglength.com/work/WRK929l"},{"title":"Large deviations of empirical neighborhood distribution in sparse random graphs",