{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiiZnW8aGQSfDYiFF1jwBs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Bollobás 1988 \"The isoperimetric number of random regular graphs\" European Journal of Combinatorics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A first order phase transition in the threshold-$\\\\theta\\\\ge 2$ contact process on random $r$-regular graphs and $r$-trees\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1011.1567\"},{\"title\":\"Metastability of the Ising model on random regular graphs at zero temperature\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.6802\"},{\"title\":\"Lower bounds for the isoperimetric numbers of random regular graphs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1311.6555\"},{\"title\":\"The Isoperimetric Number of Random Regular Graphs\",\"url\":\"https://digitalcommons.memphis.edu/facpubs/5898\"},{\"title\":\"The Isoperimetric Number of Random Regular Graphs\",\"url\":\"https://sugaku.net/oa/W1993216347\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0509022v1\"},{\"title\":\"Lower bounds for the isoperimetric numbers of random regular graphs\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.arxiv.org/html/1311.6555\"},{\"title\":\"Lower bounds for the isoperimetric numbers of random regular graphs\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/1311.6555\"},{\"title\":\"api.crossref.org\",\"url\":\"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.37236%2F651\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.00488\"}]\n\nThe 1988 paper is in the search results. It is Bollobás, \"The Isoperimetric Number of Random Regular Graphs,\" *European Journal of Combinatorics* 9(3), pp. 241–244, DOI 10.1016/S0195-6698(88)80014-3 (Bollobás, B. (1988). The Isoperimetric Number of Random Regular Graphs. European Journal of Combinatorics, 9 (3), 241-244.). The publisher's copyright is Academic Press Limited, 1988 (© 1988, Academic Press Limited.).\n\n**Main result:** The abstract says that for any positive ε there is a degree r such that almost every r-regular graph on n vertices has, for every vertex set of size at most n/2, at least (r/2 − ε)·u edges leaving that set (every set of u ⩽ n/2 vertices is joined by at least (r/2 − ε)u edges to the rest of the graph).\n\n**Method and context:** Later papers describe the paper's approach. Bollobás computed lower bounds with the first moment method for edge expansion, and he used the pairing model to do so (the pairing model, as used by Bollobás to investigate the edge isoperimetric number). A 2026 preprint credits Bollobás with introducing the pairing model and showing that expansion stays bounded away from zero with high probability for degree at least 3 (a random graph drawn from P(n,∆) has expansion bounded away from zero with high probability for any ∆ ≥ 3).\n\n**Citations:** The paper has been cited about 211 times according to one index (Citations: 211). Kolesnik and Wormald's later work on lower bounds for random regular graphs cites it as reference [5] (arXiv 1311.6555).\n\nCaveat: the search returned abstract and metadata, not the full text, so the exact constants and the proof are unverified here.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d0376bd-2c82-42d0-bb0a-a9a308847d25","uuid":"06c22b57-4885-4879-a6f3-422ea5958304","timestamp":"2026-11-01T12:38:25.832Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Bollobás 1988 \"The isoperimetric number of random regular graphs\" European Journal of Combinatorics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Lxv7x7XYpX4XX4d6TMhg5c","content":[{"title":"A first order phase transition in the threshold-$\\theta\\ge 2$ contact process on random $r$-regular graphs and $r$-trees","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1011.1567"},{"title":"Metastability of the Ising model on random regular graphs at zero temperature","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.6802"},{"title":"Lower bounds for the isoperimetric numbers of random regular graphs","url"