 Main results\n\n* `exists_prefix_closedNbhd_card_le` — for every `j ≤ n` there is a `j`-set `A`\n  with `|N[A]| ≤ j + pathwidth G`. This is Harper's vertex-isoperimetric lower\n  bound on pathwidth in its layout form (CLAUDE.md, *the expansion bound*;\n  Chandran & Kavitha 2006 on hypercubes): `pathwidth G ≥ min_{|A| = j} |N[A]| − j`\n  for every `j`.\n* `emptyPairIndex G` — `s*(G) = max_A min(|A| − 1, n − |N[A]|)`, the largest `s`\n  such that some set of at least `s + 1` vertices has at least `s` vertices\n  outside its closed neighbourhood.\n* `card_sub_two_mul_emptyPairIndex_sub_two_le_pathwidth` — **the sharp\n  empty-pair bound**: `n − 2·s*(G) − 2 ≤ pathwidth G`. Taking\n  `j = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉` in the first result gives a `j`-set with at least\n  `⌊(n − k)/2⌋ ≥ j − 1` vertices outside its closed neighbourhood, so\n  `s* ≥ j − 1`, i.e. `n − 2s* − 2 ≤ n − 2j ≤ k`.\n* `exists_empty_pair` — the survey's own phrasing: disjoint `A`, `R` with no\n  `A`–`R` edge, `|A| = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉` and `|R| ≥ ⌈(n − k)/2⌉ − 1`.\n\nThe probabilistic half (the expected number of empty pairs of these sizes in\n`G(n, c/n)` vanishes below `β*(c)·n`) is not formalised: Mathlib has no `G(n, p)`.\n-/\n\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n\n/-! ### Suffix cardinality (`card_prefixSet` is in `LinearLayout.lean`) -/\n\ntheorem card_suffixSet (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) (hi : i < Fintype.card V) :\n    (suffixSet σ i).card = Fintype.card V - (i + 1) := by\n  have := card_prefixSet_add_card_suffixSet σ i rfl\n  rw [card_prefixSet σ hi] at this\n  omega\n\n55:theorem card_suffixSet (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) (hi : i < Fintype.card V) :\n64:def inactiveSuffix (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) : Finset V :=\n67:theorem card_inactiveSuffix (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) :\n73:theorem not_adj_prefix_inactiveSuffix (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) {u v : V}\n82:theorem disjoint_prefix_inactiveSuffix (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) :\n89:def closedNbhd (A : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n92:theorem mem_closedNbhd_iff (A : Finset V) (v : V) :\n96:theorem subset_closedNbhd (A : Finset V) : A ⊆ closedNbhd G A :=\n100:theorem disjoint_closedNbhd_of_no_edge (A R : Finset V) (hAR : Disjoint A R)\n110:theorem card_closedNbhd_add_card_le (A R : Finset V) (hAR : Disjoint A R)\n120:theorem exists_empty_pair_of_layout (σ : LinearLayout V) (i : ℕ) (hi : i < Fintype.card V) :\n135:theorem exists_closedNbhd_card_le_of_layout (σ : LinearLayout V) (j : ℕ)\n149:theorem exists_closedNbhd_card_le (j : ℕ) (hj : j ≤ Fintype.card V) :\n165:def emptyPairIndex : ℕ :=\n169:theorem le_emptyPairIndex (A : Finset V) :\n175:theorem card_sub_two_mul_emptyPairIndex_sub_two_le_pathwidth :\n188:theorem exists_empty_pair (h : pathwidth G < Fintype.card V) :\n=== FirstMoment.lean\n/-\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n\n# The first-moment count: labelled graphs of small pathwidth\n\nThe counting inequality behind the first-moment lower bound on the pathwidth of\nrandom graphs (`reports/random_graph_pathwidth_survey.md` §1.4). This is step (1)\nof the plan: the finite, deterministic count. The probabilistic asymptotics —\nthat the right-hand side is `o(2^C(n,2))` below `β*(c)·n` — are step (2) and are\nnot here; Mathlib has no `G(n, p)`.\n\nChecked by brute force first (`reports/scratch/first_moment/check.py`,\n2026-10-31): every labelled graph on `1`–`6` vertices (`2^15 = 32,768` at six),\npathwidth by the subset DP, every `k < n`, zero violations of the main\ninequality and of both corollaries; `card_emptyPairGraphs` exact for every\ndisjoint `(A, R)` at `n ≤ 5` (363 pairs).\n\n## The argument\n\nWrite `n = |V|`, `C = n.choose 2`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2 = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉`. By\n`exists_empty_pair` (`EmptyPair.lean`) every graph of pathwidth `≤ k < n` has an\n*empty pair* `(A, R)` — disjoint, no `A`–`R` edge — with `|A| ≥ t` and\n`|R| ≥ t − 1`, hence one with `|A| = t`, `|R| = t − 1` exactly. The graphs with a\ngiven empty pair `(A, R)` are the edge sets inside the `C − |A|·|R|` off-diagonal\npairs not joining `A` to `R`, so there are `2^(C − |A||R|)` of them; there are\n`n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1)` pairs `(A, R)`; the union bound gives\n\n  `#{G : pathwidth G ≤ k} ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · 2^(C − t(t − 1))`.\n\n## Main results\n\n* `edges G` — the edge finset of `G`, with decidability fixed classically so that\n  `G ↦ edges G` is one injective function (`edges_injective`); `card_edges_top`\n  is Mathlib's `card_edgeFinset_top_eq_card_choose_two`.\n* `forbidden A R` — the `|A|·|R|` pairs `s(a, r)` (`card_forbidden`, for disjoint\n  `A`, `R`); `IsEmptyPair G A R` — no edge between `A` and `R`.\n* `image_edges_emptyPairGraphs` — `edges` maps the graphs with empty pair `(A, R)`\n  onto the subsets of `edges ⊤ \\ forbidden A R`, via `SimpleGraph.fromEdgeSet`.\n* `card_emptyPairGraphs` — **`#{G : IsEmptyPair G A R} = 2^(C − |A|·|R|)`**;\n  `card_simpleGraph` — **`Fintype.card (SimpleGraph V) = 2^C`**, the case\n  `A = R = ∅` (Mathlib has the `Fintype` instance but not this count).\n* `card_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le` — **the inequality above**, for any finite `V`\n  and `k < |V|`; `card_pathwidth_le_le` is the same on `Fin n`.\n* `card_pathwidth_le_mul_pow_le` — the `p = 1/2` reading, multiplied through:\n  `#{pw ≤ k} · 2^(t(t−1)) ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · 2^C`, using\n  `mul_pred_le_choose_two`, `t(t − 1) ≤ C` for `k < n`.\n* `gnpWeight p G = p^|E(G)| (1 − p)^(C − |E(G)|)`, the `G(n, p)` probability of a\n  labelled graph; `sum_gnpWeight_emptyPairGraphs` — **the `G(n, p)` probability\n  of a given empty pair `(A, R)` is `(1 − p)^(|A|·|R|)`**, by the same\n  reindexing with the binomial theorem (`Finset.sum_pow_mul_eq_add_pow`) in\n  place of `card_powerset`; `sum_biUnion_le_sum_of_nonneg` is the union bound\n  for sums of nonnegative reals, which Mathlib has only for cardinalities.\n* `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le` — **the `G(n, p)` reading**, `0 ≤ p ≤ 1`,\n  over `ℝ`: `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · (1 − p)^(t(t−1))`,\n  i.e. `P(pathwidth ≤ k) ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · (1 − p)^(t(t−1))`;\n  `weightedSum_pathwidth_le_le` is the same on `Fin n` with the weight written out.\n  Step (2) is to show this is `o(1)` at `p = c/n`, `k = βn`, `β < β*(c)`.\n\nNo `sorry`; axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only.\n81:noncomputable def edges (G : SimpleGraph V) : Finset (Sym2 V) := by\n84:theorem mem_edges {G : SimpleGraph V} {e : Sym2 V} : e ∈ edges G ↔ e ∈ G.edgeSet := by\n87:theorem edges_injective : Function.Injective (edges (V := V)) := by\n91:theorem card_edges_top : (edges (⊤ : SimpleGraph V)).card = (Fintype.card V).choose 2 := by\n95:theorem mem_edges_top {e : Sym2 V} : e ∈ edges (⊤ : SimpleGraph V) ↔ ¬ e.IsDiag := by\n99:theorem edges_subset_top (G : SimpleGraph V) : edges G ⊆ edges (⊤ : SimpleGraph V) := by\n107:def forbidden (A R : Finset V) : Finset (Sym2 V) :=\n110:theorem mem_forbidden {A R : Finset V} {e : Sym2 V} :\n119:theorem card_forbidden {A R : Finset V} (hAR : Disjoint A R) :\n129:theorem forbidden_subset_top {A R : Finset V} (hAR : Disjoint A R) :\n138:def IsEmptyPair (G : SimpleGraph V) (A R : Finset V) : Prop :=\n142:noncomputable def emptyPairGraphs (A R : Finset V) : Finset (SimpleGraph V) := by\n145:theorem mem_emptyPairGraphs {A R : Finset V} {G : SimpleGraph V} :\n149:theorem edges_subset_of_isEmptyPair {G : SimpleGraph V} {A R : Finset V}\n157:theorem edges_fromEdgeSet (S : Finset (Sym2 V)) (hS : S ⊆ edges (⊤ : SimpleGraph V)) :\n163:theorem isEmptyPair_fromEdgeSet {A R : Finset V} {S : Finset (Sym2 V)}\n171:theorem image_edges_emptyPairGraphs (A R : Finset V) :\n184:theorem card_emptyPairGraphs {A R : Finset V} (hAR : Disjoint A R) :\n190:theorem card_simpleGraph : Fintype.card (SimpleGraph V) = 2