d yields 0:31917n, Alon's upper bound yields 1:15118n, while our upper bound is\n681\t0:5028n. Furthermore, the omplementary lower bounds we get on max bise tion are well\n682\tabove the known lower bounds for all d-regular graphs, triangle-free or not.\n683\t Moreover, as an bee seen from Table 2, even for rather small values of n, the size of\n684\tthe bise tion obtained by the algorithm is lose to the solution determined by the di erential\n685\tequations. As n grows, this phenomenon strengthens.\n686\t Several open problems remain, the rst being to improve the upper bound. One way to\n687\tdo this may be to nd better priority lists. Another question is whether there is some simpler\n688\tway to analyse these greedy algorithms rigorously.\n689\tReferen es\n690\t[Alo97℄ Noga Alon. On the edge-expansion of graphs. Combinatori s, Probability and Com-\n691\t\n692\t , (6):145{152, 1997.\n693\t puting\n694\t\n695\t\n696\t[BEM 00℄ S.L. Bezroukov, R. Elsasser, B. Monien, R. Preis, and J.P. Tilli h. New spe tral\n697\t +\n698\t\n699\t lower bounds on the bise tion width of graphs. In U. Brandes and D. Wagner,\n700\t editors, 26th. Graph-Theoreti , volume 1928, pages\n701\tCon epts in Computer S ien e\n702\t\n703\t 23{34. Springer, Le ture Notes in Computer S ien e, 2000.\n704\t[Bol84℄ B. Bollob\u0013as. The isoperimetri number of random regular graphs. European Journal\n705\t\n706\t of , 9:241{244, 1984.\n707\t ombinatori s\n708\t\n709\t\n710\t[Bol01℄ B. Bollob\u0013as. Random Graphs. Se ond Edition . Combridge University Press, 2001.\n711\t[BCLS87℄ T. Bui, S. Chaudhuri, T. Leighton, and M. Sipser. Graph bise tion algorithms with\n712\t good average ase behavior. , 7:171{191, 1987.\n713\tCombinatori a\n714\t\n715\t\n716\t\n717\t10\n718\t\f[DDSW03℄ J. D\u0013\u0010az, N. Do, M. J. Serna, and N. Wormald. Bounds on the max and min bise -\n719\t tion of random ubi and random 4-regular graphs. Theorti al Computer S ien e ,\n720\t to appear, 2003.\n721\t[DPS02℄ J. D\u0013\u0010