{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgcFEpL47qCbBEtU9Fttm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 01 is complete. Everything is written, the gate passed, and the working tree holds only the item's paths.\n\n**What was done**\n\n- Read the twelve held papers in full (Lichev–Mitsche's long middle skimmed), fetched five open preprints into `literature/` with the repository's naming, and extracted text for twenty papers into `reports/scratch/separator_moment/lit/`.\n- Created `reports/separator_moment.md` with the header (three events, notation) and §1: Table A \"who counts what\", Table B \"the rates\", Table C \"representative counts and what they bought\", the brief's paragraph, what items 05–08 take from it, corrections to the item, and the non-claims.\n- Added a MISSING.md section for the five papers not obtainable without a login, each with the restatement it is cited through. All DOIs resolved through Crossref.\n\n**Main findings**\n\n- **Stop rule did not fire.** Nobody states a separator first moment for pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)` with an exact inner probability. Nearest: Do–Erde–Kang 2024 count separators with a deterministic `2^{Δ(T)|S|}` inner bound (thresholds only); Kolesnik–Wormald 2014 have the exact inner count for a single vertex cut in the configuration model.\n- **The relaxed event's rate is in print.** The LDP for the largest component (O'Connell 1998 via Puhalskii 2005, Cor. 2.4(3)) gives `P(no component > N/2) ≤ e^{−I(½)N}` with `I(½) > 0` exactly when `c′ > 2 ln 2`. Checked numerically on the quoted formula. The planner's two routes for this rate were both wrong: at `c = 6` the LDP gives 0.595 against the plan's bracket `[0.552, 1.245]`.\n- **Preview for item 06** (labelled, from the quotation alone): the relaxed separator count lifts `β*` by +0.028, +0.011, +0.004 at `c = 3, 6, 10`, and is positive for every `c > 2 ln 2`.\n- **Representative counts in print bought 1.7% to 25% of a gap** (Gao's rigid partitions, Lampis's locally optimal sets, Lichev–Mitsche's structural count).\n- **Corrections to the brief:** the Kolesnik–Wormald arXiv number was wrong; Puhalskii is in Annals of Probability; the \"Díaz–Serna–Wormald locally optimal bisections\" are actually Lampis 2012; the held Kloks preview is a different chapter.\n\n**Gate:** PASS. PROGRESS.md updated to 1/13, item marked `[x]`. Nothing committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":511458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":215,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d0376bd-2c82-42d0-bb0a-a9a308847d25","uuid":"ec0817c4-3295-4e38-b2ac-614c07ba1c96","timestamp":"2026-11-01T12:57:34.430Z","request_id":"req_011CgcFEosmpP1bWmCHneMyB"}
